== Teacher Answer Key

+ Length: metre (m); mass: kilogram (kg); time: second (s).
+ $1$ N $= 1$ kg·m/s$^2$.
+ $10^(-3)$ is milli (m); $10^(3)$ is kilo (k).
+ $3.5$ km $= 3500$ m; $250$ g $= 0.25$ kg; $45$ min $= 2700$ s.
+ $72$ km/h $= 72 times 1000 / 3600 = 20$ m/s.
+ $4.2 times 10^(-6)$ m $= 4.2$ μm.
+ $2700$ kg/m$^3 = 2.7$ g/cm$^3$ (since $1$ kg/m$^3 = 0.001$ g/cm$^3$).
+ Answers vary. Look for: a shared standard allows global comparison; a mix of units (for example, feet and metres, or Newton and pound-force) can cause calculation errors, as in the 1999 Mars Climate Orbiter loss.
+ Bonus: $850$ cm $= 8.5$ m; $0.5$ min $= 30$ s; speed $= 8.5 / 30 approx 0.28$ m/s.